0819C980 collider-target-travel-return

The division returns the travel time in r0. The clamped halfword store uses r1.

The explicit form changed the ROM bytes. The guarded form passed the unit ROM check.

--- a/src/bosses/hresvelgr/sub_0819C980.c
+++ b/src/bosses/hresvelgr/sub_0819C980.c
@@ -28,4 +28,7 @@
     result = __divsi3(distance * 628, 25600);
     SetTravelTime(actor, result);
+#ifdef UBFIX
+    return result; // preserve the inherited GBA return value
+#endif
     /* All three direct ROM callers discard the incidental return register. */
 }
